From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thuong Vo <66083331+SekiroKenjii@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 03:37:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] podman: read /etc/containers/storage.conf, not
 etc/containers/storage.conf

get_storage_directory() built the system configuration's path without its
leading slash, relative to the working directory, so it never read it. For
that file Builder takes only rootless_storage_path, which Fedora leaves
commented out, so a rootless user keeps ~/.local/share/containers/storage.
---
 src/plugins/podman/gbp-podman-runtime.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/plugins/podman/gbp-podman-runtime.c b/src/plugins/podman/gbp-podman-runtime.c
index fdf6e8a..c516da4 100644
--- a/src/plugins/podman/gbp-podman-runtime.c
+++ b/src/plugins/podman/gbp-podman-runtime.c
@@ -302,7 +302,7 @@ get_storage_directory (void)
     }
 
   /* second search for a global storage configuration */
-  global_storage_conf = g_build_filename ("etc", "containers", "storage.conf", NULL);
+  global_storage_conf = g_build_filename ("/etc", "containers", "storage.conf", NULL);
 
   if (g_file_test (global_storage_conf, G_FILE_TEST_EXISTS))
     {
